# Movement 006 source-distance tracking

Independent side-by-side read of source chapters 14–16 against manuscript chapters 38–44. Protected units, wording quoted in `MOVEMENT-006.md`, and facts or event sequences required by the packet, `BOOK_MAP.md`, or `STATE_LEDGER.md` were excluded wherever the manuscript supplied a genuinely new telling.

The requested pair-output probe was run. Its movement total (3% skeleton / 19% close) is not a count of genuine tracking: nearly all of its strongest pairs are protected exchanges, notices, findings, log entries, the Vastin window, or packet-quoted language. The overlap sweep separately reports **0 unprotected shared runs of 8+ words** and 39 protected runs. The findings below are the subtler unprotected sentence-content and beat-order matches.

## Verdict

**Seven genuine tracked passages.** Chapter 40 scene 4 is densely tracked, with two passages in the same scene. Every other affected scene contains one isolated passage, and every other scene contains none.

