    32	8. **Seln’s Path — KEEP.** It is spoken once with Oryn absent and never inferred from her unread touch (`manuscript/chapter-41.md:65–91`; `manuscript/chapter-42.md:3–11`; `manuscript/chapter-44.md:113–117`).
    33	9. **Lira’s “thirty-two” — KEEP.** It is explicitly a guess about a numeral, answered by Karis’s ignorance, not a decoded index (`manuscript/chapter-43.md:3–21`; `BOOK_MAP.md:337`).
    34	10. **Apple language — KEEP.** “A month before,” “a fortnight after,” and “before the snow’s a week old” name neither a month nor a season, do not count back to a birthday, and fit the established frost/cold-road weather before snow (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:75–111,275–289`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:487,573`).
    35	11. **“The last time” — KEEP.** It supplies no interval to the former birthday (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:185–193,311`).
    36	12. **Founding stone — KEEP, with reserved-agency repairs 11–12.** The old gate footing and civic dating custom contradict no bible, map or later packet and give no numerical year (`manuscript/chapter-42.md:205–217`; `BOOK_MAP.md:333–334`).
    37	13. **Length — KEEP.** The 37,523-word movement is about four percent over the target, with the five findings and required windows present (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:7,16–24,37–41`). This is not a canon or plan failure.
    38	14. **Reader grade — KEEP.** The first scene states harm, touch, conditions and cost in direct concrete language and withholds forgiveness; the reported grade is 3.44 (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:105–179,203–249`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:11`).
