    17	
    18	## Where we enter
    19	
    20	The Stair's rim on the 115th, with a bearing taken off two sites with a brass edge. Brom's shoulder is mended once, and Lira's arm is closed again. Six people and two mules. Teague's crew is turning back toward Millrace.
    21	
    22	## What this movement is for
    23	
    24	The found family's together-fight, terrain-first and Pathless. The still place told, with the reader's hand on the healer's wrist. The book's moral stake paid by *not* reading a man. Four sites on a line. First snow, a ledger that admits it is too small, and a sixth chair filled by post. Turns and promises:
    25	
    26	- **The bearing walk (116–118), on the page:** a road, then a track, then a carter's memory. Karis does not once say *if*. The country going into the last mild days. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]
    27	- **The Drowned Hall from the rise:** roofless, twelve strides square, a spring through the broken floor, a marsh exactly as wide as the Quiet. "Third." **The line** at the marsh's edge ("Gone"/"Back"); **stake thirty-three** (old, and no second); mud **heaved from below** along the water's edge ("It's never been out."); a bar at the hall's lip **bent from below**, read from a hundred and eighty-five yards. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] **Oryn's lore**: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole."
    28	- **The trials (≈2,500), from the hall's outer coping inside the perimeter (EXC-B7-005):** the causeway crossing, with her hands checked at the stride both ways; the rule walking with them; the bulge once in a quarter-hour; a stone at eleven; Lira's skipping stone answered only where it stops, at fourteen; **Seln's rule in his own hand on Karis's page** ("It's blind… it strikes what *stays*."); **Cael's Anchor point** held for sixty counts ("It reads that as the heaviest thing…" / "…the thing that *stays*."). The council at the stone (protected Lira lines). Camp at the line.
    29	- **Day 119, the Hall (≈5,000–6,000):** Brom *stops* to put Karis up the wall and the floor opens under him; he puts her up before he goes sideways. "Get *off* the floor." **The coping** as cover and trap. Karis copying the wall she kneels on, funny for exactly one exchange. **Brom's shoulder opens**; he slips on the wrong wall. **Oryn into the water, skipping**, the healer reaching a falling patient (not heroic, only nearest). **The second pass turns** toward where she is going. **Cael in, declaring:** Compression takes the strike into a standing frame at the broken edge; **Anchor laid on the floor** at the broken centre. "A thing that hunts what stays commits to the thing that stays hardest." It surfaces whole for the first time in anyone's memory. "Brom. Wall. Your weight. Now." **Four bolts into the pale**: Lira twice, braced one-armed against the coping and a knee, with Seln spanning between (the bowman's lessons pay); Seln twice. The point released; the jaws close on water; it lets go and goes down, alive. "Walls… Twelve sheets." It is left there.
    30	- **Costs at the track's end:** Oryn's hour, "Twice…" (protected); the long sit, wet to the waist; his bill (Compression in the ribs, Anchor held against biting, the read at its dearest under water). **The exchange** (protected) ending "Lie still. I want to read you."
    31	- **Two days at the marsh (119–120):** two fires. Seln's blanket over Karis's shoulders. Lira keeps the bolt in the bow. Brom: "Twice." / "Twice." Oryn sleeps in front of people. **The second self-reading** (an hour; the banks a limit; **the still place**, named here for the first time; the river round a stone it has always known; four things he can count; protected log). The third before dawn: "the same." **Oryn changes the order**: "You in me." Asked and granted; surface, then a minute of the long one at her count, and while he is in, **he tells her exactly**; her finding (protected); "Write it down and stop touching it." **C3: Karis lays the cord at the Hall's perimeter** in the marsh between copies. **Teague's crew** along the track with a fifth: the older healer of no Path, "Twice?" / "Then it wants binding, not hands." The two women bind it. **Teague sits down beside him**, as Brom once did. "What are you." **The wrist a foot from his hand:** not the short reading, not the long one, not the asking. "Why did you stop reporting?" (protected exchange). "The board's going to need a new column." The log (protected). **The pencil stopping** at the far fire.
    32	- **Day 121, the finding:** "Three points make a line. Four make an argument." The kit's bearing is the same line. The fourth circle is three days out. "I'm telling you where I'll be." / "That's a healer's sentence." / "I know whose it is."
    33	- **The walk (121–122):** frost that rings; one cart of hides and a lifted hand; holds shut; the six catalogued because they will be five; the first night in a ruined hold's lee ("Twice." / "Twice." / "And not three."). **The fork:** "three weeks late there… I'm going back to being the route." He walks her fifty paces and does not ask. "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." **The four behind him, with one mule.** The log at the fork (protected).
    34	- **Five on the bearing (122–123):** the ridge with white lines in its folds; Seln's "Nothing" every hour; **"I love this country."** at noon, with the dread in the same coat. **The fourth site from the crest at dusk:** "Larger." A valley head; a standing grey shape taller than a man, neither ring nor stair, that the dusk keeps. Lira's *gone* at about a hundred and ninety paces, not forty. Twenty cords paced along the line from outside, half the bend: four hundred. **The cordon**, iron a pace apart, numbered thirty-four with the stroke and the bar, both ways (forty counted, and more). "That's not a survey. That's a cordon…" **The council: five voices and one silence** (protected). Nobody crosses. Camp on the crest; the log (protected).
    35	- **Home (124–129), on the page:** six days into first snow; the ribs in the cold, then quiet by the marsh's count; **Seln gives Karis the ledger** on the road and does not ask for it back; Lira's taped foot put down flat, the word *ankle* never said.
    36	- **Lowmarch (129–131):** the fifth honest catalogue, from the landing. **The season line read** (protected); the ledger turned toward him; **no number**; "too small" (protected); the room's "Eleventh." / "Aye." **Teague's term** and "Noted." The healer's single look at Brom's shoulder. **The cold-term fence** given over ("Ours.") [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]. Karis takes the back room and pays without counting (ninety-six). **The inventory** (protected; the audio rule). **The last ferry**: nine pieces sorted aloud; **Hesk's straightedge** with the note (protected); the replies west (protected). **Oryn's letter by carter** the morning after (protected): "Six, by letter." "She'll say when." / "After the thaw." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] **The map**: four circles, the bearing, both edges laid along it, **touching the three paced centres for Cael exactly as for Karis**. "The sites were on an alignment. Not random." "Someone made this pattern." Four seconds. **The closing, exact.**
