   633	- **What she felt in the long reading (flag):** near the end, something kept pace beside her, with her own short step on the right; then it was in him, going by itself.
   634	- **The listening (flag):** his own current at the edge of every thought, quick and slow; the nine by sound (Wind, dry grass going over; the read, a millstone through a floor; Ember, a wick ticking; Pressure, a bellows; Compression, hemp under load; Anchor, one held note; Blade, a wet finger on a glass; Shadow, a hush that drops the others; Storm, a sea turning over). It cannot be refused, since it asks for nothing. Three nights.
   635	- **Storm resettling (flag):** heard as one long roll from side to side; afterward the ground arrives half a beat late until dusk, with no lane laid.
