   640	- **The yard bow (flag):** the hold's old stirrup crossbow, kept under the gate-walk in a goatskin "for the fox"; a belt hook; eight blunt bolts fletched with goose feather; it throws left. A straw sack on a stake outside the west gate, forty paces and then sixty, shot at noon. Lira's scores: none of eight in the ring (the 104th); two (the 106th); five from the rail and three from the knee (the 108th); four of eight from the rail and one of one from the knee at sixty (the 110th). The bowman's rail is worn hollow by thirty years of his left hand; nothing has come up to the white stone for fifty-seven evenings; he leaves Lira the walk at dusk on the 110th.
